assifier is constructed and applied to data; u.d.<bold>=</bold> user-defined. <bold>Bias:</bold> Bias of the error estimation; &#x02191; means positive bias, i.e. underestimation of prediction accuracy and vice-versa. <bold>Principle:</bold> Gives the definition of the learning and test sets or the used combination of methods.</p></caption><table frame="hsides" rules="groups"><thead><tr><th align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1"/><th align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Iterations</th><th align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Bias</th><th align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Principle</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Resubstitution</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">1</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">&#x02193;</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1"><bold>l</bold> = <bold>t</bold> = {1, &#x02026;, <italic>n</italic>}</td></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Test</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">1</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">&#x02191;</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">{<bold>l</bold>, <bold>t</bold>} from a partition of {1, &#x02026;, <italic>n</italic>}</td></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">LOOCV</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1"><italic>n</italic></td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1"><italic>&#x02013;</italic></td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1"><bold>t</bold><sup>(</sup><italic><sup>j</sup></italic><sup>)</sup> = {<italic>j</italic> }, <bold>l</bold><sup>(</sup><italic><sup>j</sup></italic><sup>)</sup> = {1, &#x02026;, <italic>n</italic>}\{<italic>j</italic> },for <italic>j</italic> = 1, &#x02026;, <italic>n</italic></td></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">m-fold-CV</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1"><italic>m</italic></td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">&#x02191;</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1"><bold>t</bold><sup>(1)</sup>, &#x02026;, <bold>t</bold><sup>(</sup><italic><sup>m</sup></italic><sup>)</sup> from a partition of {1, &#x02026;, <italic>n</italic>}<break/><bold>l</bold><sup>(</sup><italic><sup>j</sup></italic><sup>)</sup> = {1, &#x02026;, <italic>n</italic>}\ <bold>t</bold><sup>(</sup><italic><sup>j</sup></italic><sup>)</sup>, for <italic>j</italic> =1, &#x02026;, <italic>m</italic>}</td></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">MCCV</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">B (u.d.)</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">&#x02191;</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">{<bold>l</bold><sup>(</sup><italic><sup>b</sup></italic><sup>)</sup>, <bold>t</bold><sup>(</sup><italic><sup>b</sup></italic><sup>)</sup>} from a partition of {1, &#x02026;, <italic>n</italic>}, for <italic>b</italic> = 1, &#x02026;, <italic>B</italic></td></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Bootstrap</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">B (u.d.)</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">&#x02191;</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1"><bold>l</bold><sup>*(</sup><italic><sup>b</sup></italic><sup>)</sup> is a bootstrap sample drawn out of {1, &#x02026;, <italic>n</italic>}<break/><bold>t</bold><sup>*(</sup><italic><sup>b</sup></italic><sup>)</sup><italic>=</italic> {1, &#x02026;, <italic>n</italic>}\<bold>l</bold><sup>*(</sup><italic><sup>b</sup></italic><sup>)</sup>, for <italic>b</italic> = 1, &#x02026;, <italic>B</italic></td></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">0.632,0.632+</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">B (u.d.)</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1"><italic>&#x02013;</italic></td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Weighted sum of resubstitution and bootstrap error rates.</td></tr><tr><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Bootstrap-CV</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1"><italic>n</italic>B (u.d)</td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1"><italic>&#x02013;</italic></td><td align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">LOOCV within <italic>B</italic> boo